diff --git a/docs/bots.md b/docs/bots.md
index ed70ba5..2e426c8 100644
--- a/docs/bots.md
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -27,7 +27,16 @@ Responses:
 
 Bots are users with a separate `bot` role and a creator. This reuses avatars,
 room membership controls, message authorship, unread broadcasts, and push jobs.
-New bots join existing open rooms, and new open rooms include existing bots.
+New bots do **not** join any rooms by default. People still automatically join
+all open rooms. Both bot forms have an **Add to all open rooms** checkbox, off by
+default. Enabling it joins every existing open room and all future open rooms
+(including closed rooms converted to open). Disabling it keeps current
+memberships and stops automatic joins. Existing bots and memberships are
+preserved on upgrade; the new preference defaults to off for existing bots too.
+
+Room administrators can select individual bots using the room's access
+checkboxes, in both open and closed rooms. In open rooms, people and opted-in
+bots always have access; only other bots have editable membership checkboxes.
 They are excluded from account role controls and password login. Their empty
 password digest is deliberate: they do not have a password.
 
@@ -35,6 +44,38 @@ Deletion follows the existing user deactivation behavior: it removes shared
 room memberships and revokes API access immediately, but keeps earlier
 messages and their author names. A deleted bot is omitted from management.
 
+## Joining rooms
+
+When an active bot with a webhook first joins a non-direct room, Campfire queues
+a `POST` with `Content-Type: application/json` after the membership commits:
+
+```json
+{
+  "event": "joined",
+  "room": {
+    "id": 5,
+    "name": "Ops",
+    "reply_to": "/rooms/5/BOT_CODE/messages"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Both automatic and manual grants use this path. Direct conversations never
+send `joined`. A `200` text or HTML response posts a message as the bot in that
+room, exactly as for mentions below; `204` acknowledges without a reply.
+
+A unique `Room::BotJoin` record for each bot/room pair prevents duplicate events
+from repeated grants, room edits/conversions, toggling the preference, or even
+removing and re-adding the bot. These records survive membership removal and are
+deleted with the bot or room. Rolled-back memberships do not record or notify a
+join. Configuring a webhook later does not replay historical joins.
+
